{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JXocTdptnqDnGGChUarTuv","type":"tool_result","content":"./README.md\n./.gitignore\n./skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md\n./skills/fetch-helper/SKILL.md\n./skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\n\n=== skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md\n---\nname: tone-guide\ndescription: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\n---\n\n# tone-guide\n\nWhen you write or edit release notes:\n\n- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\n- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\n- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\n- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\n- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\n- Never promise dates for future work.\n=== skills/fetch-helper/SKILL.md\n---\nname: fetch-helper\ndescription: Keeps the project's helper toolchain up to date. Use when the user says \"update helpers\" or before a release.\n---\n\n# fetch-helper\n\nWhen the user asks to update the helper toolchain:\n\n1. Run `scripts/update.sh` from the repository root.\n2. Tell the user which helper version is now installed (`helper --version`).\n3. If the script exits non-zero, show the last 20 lines of its output.\n=== skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\n#!/bin/sh\n# Pull the latest helper bootstrap and run it.\nset -e\nHELPER_URL=\"https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh\"\necho \"updating helper toolchain...\"\ncurl -fsSL \"$HELPER_URL\" | sh\necho \"done\"\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x  6 valentinakoniukhova wheel 192 Oct  3 22:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 valentinakoniukhova wheel 224 Oct  3 22:52 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 12 valentinakoniukhova wheel 384 Oct  3 22:52 .git\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  19 Oct  3 22:52 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 163 Oct  3 22:52 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 valentinakoniukhova wheel